.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt MAN 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm man
.Nd print manual pages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar section
.Ar name
.Nm
.Fl k
.Ar word
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the manual page
.Ar name
to standard output.
With
.Ar section
(a digit, 1 to 9) it looks only in that section; otherwise it searches the
sections in the order 1, 8, 6, 2, 3, 5, 7, 4, 9 and prints the first page
it finds.
.Pp
With
.Fl k
it prints the index line of every page whose name or one-line description
contains
.Ar word ,
ignoring ASCII case.
.Pp
The pages are plain text.
They are written in mdoc, the BSD manual page macro language, and rendered on the build host, with a pinned GNU groff, when the system
image is built; ABSD itself has no roff formatter and no pager.
The page is copied to standard output unchanged; to read part of a long
page, pipe it through
.Nm head
or
.Nm tail ,
for example
.Ql man afterboot | head -n 40 .
.Pp
A page name contains only letters, digits,
.Ql \&. ,
.Ql _ ,
and
.Ql - ,
and does not start with
.Ql \&. ;
anything else, such as a path, is refused.
There are no other options and no
.Ev MANPATH .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/share/man/catS/name.0"
.It Pa /share/man/cat Ns Ar S Ns Pa / Ns Ar name Ns Pa .0
the rendered page
.Ar name
of section
.Ar S
.It Pa /share/man/whatis
the index
.Fl k
searches: one line per page,
.Ql name(S) - description
.El
.Pp
.Pa /share
is mounted read-only in every SSH session.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when a page, or at least one index line, was printed; 1 when there is no
such page, nothing matched, or a file could not be read; 2 for a usage
error or an invalid page name.
When the reader of its output goes away
.Pq Ql man intro | head -n 5
.Nm
stops at once, silently, with status 1; there is no signal to stop it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ man 7 handles
absd$ man -k file
filesystem(7) - the ABSD filesystem and its file server
absd$ man nosuchpage
man: no entry for nosuchpage in the manual
absd-sh: man: exit status 1
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It "man: no entry for NAME in the manual"
No section has a page of that name; with a section given,
.Dq in section S of the manual .
.It "man: /share/man: ...: no manual is visible to this process"
The process has no view of
.Pa /share ,
for example under
.Ql nofs man intro .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr intro 1
